@workspace twixy

SKILL "KPI Report"
  version: 1.0
  summary: "수집된 워크스페이스 데이터를 읽어 기간별 KPI를 집계·분석하고 PDF 또는 Google Sheet 리포트로 발행한다."
  description: "Aggregates the marketing data already sitting in the workspace (data/raw, data/insights) into a period-over-period KPI summary and ships it as a PDF or a Google Sheet. Composition only — no new tools: tool-read-xlsx / read for the raw data, an LLM sub-agent for aggregation + narrative, and tool-write-pdf or tool-write-gsheet for the deliverable. The marketer supplies the period, which channels/metrics to roll up, and the output format; the skill returns the report path (or Sheet URL) plus a short headline of the key movements. Pair it with a cron schedule (e.g. schedule: \"0 9 * * 1\") to get a standing weekly/monthly KPI report with no manual trigger. Trigger phrases: KPI 리포트, 성과 집계, 주간 리포트, 월간 리포트, 지표 정리해줘, kpi report, performance summary, weekly report, metrics roundup."
  tags: [reporting, kpi, analytics, pdf, sheets, deliverable]
  trigger: "KPI 리포트, KPI 집계, 성과 리포트, 주간 리포트, 월간 리포트, 지표 정리, 성과 요약, kpi report, performance report, weekly report, monthly report, metrics summary"
  output: "KPI report PDF in $REPORTS or Google Sheet URL + headline summary; emits kpi_report_ready"

PLATFORMS {
  INSTAGRAM
  TIKTOK
  LINKEDIN
  TWITTER
  YOUTUBE
}

GOAL "Roll collected data into a period KPI report" {
  objective: "Read the marketing data already in the workspace, aggregate the requested KPIs for the requested period (with period-over-period deltas), and publish a clean PDF or Google Sheet the marketer can share."
  kpi: kpi_reports_shipped
  window: 7 days
}

PHASE "Scope" {
  COLLECT "Resolve scope and load the source data" {
    // Decide what to report on before reading anything.
    - Resolve report scope from the user's request (infer sensible defaults — do not over-ask):
      period: reporting window, e.g. last 7 days / last 30 days / a month name. Default: last 7 days.
      channels: which platforms to include. Default: every channel present in the data.
      metrics: which KPIs to roll up — reach, impressions, engagement_rate, followers, views, etc. Default: the core set available in the source.
      format: "pdf" (share-ready) or "sheet" (further pivoting). Default: pdf.
      data location: where the source lives. Default: data/insights/ first, then data/raw/.

    // Source the actual numbers. Prefer structured files; fall back to raw.
    LOAD "latest" FROM $INSIGHTS AS $insight_data
    - If the source is an .xlsx, call tool-read-xlsx with relPath = the file under data/raw/ or data/insights/. It returns { sheets: [{ name, rows }] } (first 200 rows/sheet).
    - If the source is markdown/JSON, read the relevant files under $RAW / $INSIGHTS directly.
    - If no data is found for the period, abort with a friendly message telling the user to collect it first (Data Scout) — do NOT fabricate numbers.
  }
}

PHASE "Aggregate" {
  ANALYZE "Compute KPIs and write the narrative" {
    SPAWN kpi_aggregator
      TASK "Aggregate the source data into the requested KPIs for the requested period. For each metric: total (or average for rate metrics), the value for the prior comparable period, and the delta (absolute + %). Break the numbers down by channel when channel data is present. Then write a short narrative: 3-5 bullets on what moved and the single most important finding. Return a normalized payload with (1) kpi_rows for tabular output — array of { metric, channel, value, prior, delta_pct } with a header row first, and (2) report_blocks for PDF — array of { type:'h1'|'h2'|'p'|'bullet'|'table', ... } with the headline, the narrative bullets, and the KPI table. Do not invent metrics absent from the source; mark missing values N/A."
      USING $insight_data
      OUTPUT $kpi
      AWAIT

    STORE $kpi AS "kpi_aggregate_{date}" IN $INSIGHTS
  }
}

PHASE "Publish" {
  TRACK "Write the report and announce the path" {
    LET $stem = "kpi_report_{period}_{date}"

    // Two output paths — pick by $format. PDF is local; Sheet needs Google.
    - If format == "pdf": call tool-write-pdf with relPath = "$REPORTS/{stem}.pdf" and payload = { title: "KPI Report — {period}", blocks: $kpi.report_blocks }. The handler returns { ok, relPath, bytes }.
    - If format == "sheet": first call tool-google-status; if !connected, abort with a friendly message pointing to Settings → Google Workspace → Connect. If connected, call tool-write-gsheet with payload = { title: "KPI Report — {period}", sheets: [{ name: "KPIs", rows: $kpi.kpi_rows }] }. The handler returns { ok, spreadsheetId, url, sheets } — use $url verbatim.

    - Report to the user: the relative report path (e.g. data/reports/kpi_report_last-7-days_2026-06-26.pdf) or the Google Sheet URL, plus the one-line headline finding from the aggregation.
    - When this skill runs on a cron schedule, the same report regenerates automatically each period — surface the new path/URL in the scheduled-run notification.

    EMIT "kpi_report_ready"
      WITH payload = { stem: $stem, format: $format, period: $period }
      TO SKILL "Watchtower"
  }
}
